WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.747
-Today is Friday and that's

00:00:01.747 --> 00:00:03.002
usually when I catch up

00:00:03.002 --> 00:00:04.003
with some personal stuff,
you know, I

00:00:04.003 --> 00:00:05.004
check my inbox and return

00:00:05.004 --> 00:00:06.272
some emails and, of course,

00:00:06.272 --> 00:00:08.107
I send out thank-you notes.

00:00:08.107 --> 00:00:10.176
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:00:10.176 --> 00:00:13.146
I was running behind today,
so I thought,

00:00:13.146 --> 00:00:14.647
if you guys wouldn't mind,
I'd like to write out

00:00:14.647 --> 00:00:16.483
my weekly thank-you notes
right now.

00:00:16.483 --> 00:00:17.549
Is that cool with you guys?

00:00:17.549 --> 00:00:19.051
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:00:19.051 --> 00:00:20.920
I appreciate it.
James, can I get

00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:22.622
some thank-you note writing
music, please?

00:00:22.622 --> 00:00:23.990
[ Playing tender tune ]

00:00:23.990 --> 00:00:25.725
[ Laughter ]

00:00:25.725 --> 00:00:26.893
-Oh, boy.

00:00:26.893 --> 00:00:27.994
-Good, isn't it?

00:00:27.994 --> 00:00:31.630
♪♪

00:00:31.630 --> 00:00:34.501
Thank you,
this year's Oscars set,

00:00:34.501 --> 00:00:35.735
for looking like you were filmed

00:00:35.735 --> 00:00:37.771
in IKEA's outdoor
furniture section.

00:00:37.771 --> 00:00:40.472
[ Laughter, cheering,
and applause ]

00:00:40.472 --> 00:00:42.542
That's real.
-IKEA, yes.

00:00:42.542 --> 00:00:43.709
[ Laughter ]

00:00:43.709 --> 00:00:44.877
♪♪

00:00:44.877 --> 00:00:46.913
-Thank you,
Oscar-nominated movies

00:00:46.913 --> 00:00:49.049
that were only released
on streaming,

00:00:49.049 --> 00:00:50.917
or, as straight-to-DVD
movies put it,

00:00:50.917 --> 00:00:53.453
"Oh, so, now,
this is a celebrated thing?"

00:00:53.453 --> 00:00:54.454
[ Laughter, cheering,
and applause ]

00:00:54.454 --> 00:00:56.388
"Okay.

00:00:56.388 --> 00:00:59.125
Okay."
[ Laughter ]

00:00:59.125 --> 00:01:00.393
-Wow!

00:01:00.393 --> 00:01:02.762
-"So, now, it's
a celebrated thing? Okay."

00:01:02.762 --> 00:01:04.830
[ Laughter ]

00:01:04.830 --> 00:01:06.866
-Rules got changed.

00:01:06.866 --> 00:01:10.136
-"Okay. We're doing that,
now, I guess. Okay."

00:01:10.136 --> 00:01:12.705
[ Laughter ]

00:01:12.705 --> 00:01:13.773
♪♪

00:01:13.773 --> 00:01:15.174
Thank you, AirTag,

00:01:15.174 --> 00:01:18.611
for being the name
of Apple's new device tracker,

00:01:18.611 --> 00:01:21.314
as well as a great game idea
for an only child.

00:01:21.314 --> 00:01:22.882
[ Laughter, cheering,
and applause ]
Billy, go outside

00:01:22.882 --> 00:01:25.618
and play AirTag.

00:01:25.618 --> 00:01:26.919
"You're it, air!

00:01:26.919 --> 00:01:30.423
[ Laughter ]
Okay, we're doing that, now?

00:01:30.423 --> 00:01:34.460
Okay, okay.

00:01:34.460 --> 00:01:36.362
-Just not liking it.
-Oh, we're doing that, now?

00:01:36.362 --> 00:01:38.264
Okay."

00:01:38.264 --> 00:01:39.532
[ Laughter ]

00:01:39.532 --> 00:01:42.000
-God.

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:43.168
-You're overreacting.

00:01:43.168 --> 00:01:44.370
-"No, no."

00:01:44.370 --> 00:01:46.439
-"Oh, we're doing that, now,
I guess. Okay."

00:01:46.439 --> 00:01:47.640
♪♪

00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:51.043
Thank you, Stouffer's
new lasagna mac,

00:01:51.043 --> 00:01:52.879
for being the tastiest way
to let people know

00:01:52.879 --> 00:01:54.179
you're going through
some stuff right now.

00:01:54.179 --> 00:01:56.148
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:56.148 --> 00:01:59.685
Just get off my back.

00:01:59.685 --> 00:02:02.789
Looks pretty good to me, man.

00:02:02.789 --> 00:02:03.856
Do you think you
can taste the difference

00:02:03.856 --> 00:02:05.825
between the cheese and sauce,

00:02:05.825 --> 00:02:08.560
than the mac,
the cheddar cheese?

00:02:08.560 --> 00:02:09.929
-You mean the mac cheese?

00:02:09.929 --> 00:02:12.265
It's lasagna mac, so it's made
with macaroni &amp; cheese,

00:02:12.265 --> 00:02:14.133
but lasagna-style.
-It's lasagna, but,

00:02:14.133 --> 00:02:17.637
in the middle of the lasagna is
macaroni &amp; cheese.

00:02:17.637 --> 00:02:19.072
-Yeah, I think I could tell.

00:02:19.072 --> 00:02:20.539
[ Laughter ]

00:02:20.539 --> 00:02:23.375
I have a food problem,
so I'm sure I could tell.

00:02:23.375 --> 00:02:24.376
-You have what?

00:02:24.376 --> 00:02:25.711
-A food problem.
I love food.

00:02:25.711 --> 00:02:27.447
[ Laughter ]
-A food problem?

00:02:27.447 --> 00:02:28.715
-Yeah.

00:02:28.715 --> 00:02:29.982
Problem with food.

00:02:29.982 --> 00:02:31.417
-What's the problem?

00:02:31.417 --> 00:02:33.853
I said I'm on a seafood diet.

00:02:33.853 --> 00:02:34.853
-Oh, my gosh.
-Yeah.

00:02:34.853 --> 00:02:36.289
-You "see food,"
you eat it, right?

00:02:36.289 --> 00:02:38.724
-No, no, no. Fish, shellfish.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:38.724 --> 00:02:40.760
-Oh.
-You know, clams. Trying to keep
the cholesterol down.

00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:42.128
-Sorry.
I misunderstood.

00:02:42.128 --> 00:02:43.930
I thought you were making a --
-Oh, you thought I said

00:02:43.930 --> 00:02:46.932
"s-e-e" diet.
-[ English accent ] Well,
I thought you were,

00:02:46.932 --> 00:02:48.134
perhaps, doing

00:02:48.134 --> 00:02:49.802
-A comical bit?
-some humor.

00:02:49.802 --> 00:02:53.506
-No. I was merely telling you
a fact about my, uh,

00:02:53.506 --> 00:02:54.840
dietary means.

00:02:54.840 --> 00:02:56.709
-No, understood.
I thought you said

00:02:56.709 --> 00:02:57.844
you're on a "see food" diet
-I did.

00:02:57.844 --> 00:02:58.945
-and you going
to finish it up with,

00:02:58.945 --> 00:03:00.946
"I see food, I eat it."
But, instead,

00:03:00.946 --> 00:03:01.981
you're on a seafood diet.
Of course, you're talking

00:03:01.981 --> 00:03:03.315
about shrimp and trout,

00:03:03.315 --> 00:03:05.451
maybe sea bass, maybe.
-Yes.

00:03:05.451 --> 00:03:09.422
-Maybe a thick sea bass.
-Thick, thick chunk of sea bass.

00:03:09.422 --> 00:03:11.424
-Yes.
-With some chili mac over it.

00:03:11.424 --> 00:03:15.794
-Yes. Or some of the whole fish
under salt.

00:03:15.794 --> 00:03:17.363
[ Italian accent ]
Branzino!

00:03:17.363 --> 00:03:18.831
[ Laughter ]

00:03:18.831 --> 00:03:21.667
For two!
-[ Italian accent ]
 Due branzini!

00:03:21.667 --> 00:03:23.403
 -Due branzini!

00:03:23.403 --> 00:03:25.070
[ Laughter ]

00:03:25.070 --> 00:03:26.538
-[ English accent ]
Can you smother that

00:03:26.538 --> 00:03:29.142
with some Stouffer's
lasagna mac?
[ Laughter ]

00:03:29.142 --> 00:03:30.209
-[ English accent ]
Can you take this fish

00:03:30.209 --> 00:03:32.145
and just completely ruin it

00:03:32.145 --> 00:03:35.415
by putting microwave
pasta on top, but then --

00:03:35.415 --> 00:03:36.849
[ Laughter ]

00:03:36.849 --> 00:03:39.251
I think it's a mistake.

00:03:39.251 --> 00:03:41.654
I think the lasagna's one thing
and I'm down for Stouffer's.

00:03:41.654 --> 00:03:44.223
I'm a French bread pizza dude.
I love those.

00:03:44.223 --> 00:03:45.524
-Sure.
Yeah, I'm all for that.

00:03:45.524 --> 00:03:46.726
-Lasagna? Sure. Get it.

00:03:46.726 --> 00:03:48.795
Mac &amp; cheese? Sure.
-Together? Good.

00:03:48.795 --> 00:03:50.963
-No, I think it's a mistake.
It's the same.

00:03:50.963 --> 00:03:52.765
It's going to destroy
the flavors. It's -- No.

00:03:52.765 --> 00:03:54.801
-You think it might even
take down lasagna.

00:03:54.801 --> 00:03:56.902
-Yeah, I think I might
take it out. Take it down.

00:03:56.902 --> 00:03:59.839
-They wouldn't do that
in Naples, in Napoli.

00:03:59.839 --> 00:04:01.907
-Oh, they'd get so mad.
-Yeah. They'd be like --

00:04:01.907 --> 00:04:04.977
[ Italian accent ]
Branzini!

00:04:04.977 --> 00:04:06.879
-[ Italian accent ]
What are you doing?!

00:04:06.879 --> 00:04:10.616
[ Falsetto faux Italian ]

00:04:10.616 --> 00:04:14.553
[ Baritone
faux Italian ]

00:04:14.553 --> 00:04:16.455
[ Falsetto faux Italian ]

00:04:16.455 --> 00:04:18.457
[ Baritone
faux Italian ]

00:04:18.457 --> 00:04:20.692
[ Creaky faux Italian ]

00:04:20.692 --> 00:04:23.362
[ Baritone
faux Italian ]

00:04:23.362 --> 00:04:24.831
-Stouffer's.

00:04:24.831 --> 00:04:27.567
[ Laughter ]

00:04:27.567 --> 00:04:28.568
[ Applause ]

00:04:28.568 --> 00:04:30.936
That's a weird ad.
-Yeah. Odd ad.

00:04:30.936 --> 00:04:32.405
That was a commercial
for Stouffer's?

00:04:32.405 --> 00:04:34.306
-Yeah, it was
a commercial for Stouffer's.

00:04:34.306 --> 00:04:36.209
-People in Italy arguing?
-Yeah, they're arguing

00:04:36.209 --> 00:04:37.676
about how...
-They woke the grandma.

00:04:37.676 --> 00:04:39.345
-Yeah, they woke Grandma up
out of bed.

00:04:39.345 --> 00:04:41.748
[ Laughter ]

00:04:41.748 --> 00:04:43.382
Are we on "Popular Mathematics"?
-What's that?

00:04:43.382 --> 00:04:45.184
Yeah. No, no,
we're doing a different bit --

00:04:45.184 --> 00:04:47.219
thank-you notes.
-Oh, sorry.
I zoned out for a sec.

00:04:47.219 --> 00:04:48.788
No problem, bud.
[ Chuckle ]

00:04:48.788 --> 00:04:50.289
[ Laughter ]

00:04:50.289 --> 00:04:51.657
♪♪
[ Laughter ]

00:04:51.657 --> 00:04:53.792
Thank you, giant explosions,

00:04:53.792 --> 00:04:55.527
for meaning one
of three things --

00:04:55.527 --> 00:04:56.729
a fire, a gas leak,

00:04:56.729 --> 00:04:58.398
or a gender reveal gone wrong.

00:04:58.398 --> 00:05:00.366
[ Cheering and applause ]
No, that's too real.

00:05:00.366 --> 00:05:05.304
[ Applause ]

00:05:05.304 --> 00:05:06.739
♪♪

00:05:06.739 --> 00:05:10.843
Thank you, Natty Light's
new frozen icicles,

00:05:10.843 --> 00:05:12.378
for not going
by your original name --

00:05:12.378 --> 00:05:13.679
Go-gurt for Drunks.

00:05:13.679 --> 00:05:16.882
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:16.882 --> 00:05:18.851
-Natty Light!
-Natty Light, yeah.

00:05:18.851 --> 00:05:20.986
That makes anyone --

00:05:20.986 --> 00:05:22.755
If you call Natural Light
Natty Light,

00:05:22.755 --> 00:05:24.590
it's your first Light.
-That should say something
about you.

00:05:24.590 --> 00:05:27.359
-How many Stouffer's macs
do you got? Oh.

00:05:27.359 --> 00:05:28.995
-"They're even better
non-frozen."

00:05:28.995 --> 00:05:30.129
[ Laughter ]

00:05:30.129 --> 00:05:31.263
-You were eating them frozen?

00:05:31.263 --> 00:05:32.831
-They're just beer?

00:05:32.831 --> 00:05:34.500
"Yeah, beer in a tube.

00:05:34.500 --> 00:05:36.102
They should put it in a can."

00:05:36.102 --> 00:05:37.303
[ Laughter ]

00:05:37.303 --> 00:05:39.005
-"Then, you can drink it
all day long."

00:05:39.005 --> 00:05:40.740
[ Laughter ]

00:05:40.740 --> 00:05:41.907
♪♪

00:05:41.907 --> 00:05:44.476
-Thank you,
white noise machines,

00:05:44.476 --> 00:05:45.978
for getting me to pay $80,

00:05:45.978 --> 00:05:48.046
when it could've just put
a bucket over a fan.

00:05:48.046 --> 00:05:54.053
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:54.053 --> 00:05:55.120
Was that your
white noise machine?

00:05:55.120 --> 00:05:58.458
-Yeah.
[ Whirring ]

00:05:58.458 --> 00:05:59.759
Pbbbt!

00:05:59.759 --> 00:06:02.227
[ Laughter ]

00:06:02.227 --> 00:06:03.296
Pbbt!
♪♪

00:06:03.296 --> 00:06:04.963
[ Laughter ]

00:06:04.963 --> 00:06:06.098
Pbbt!
♪♪

00:06:06.098 --> 00:06:08.300
-Come on, dude.

00:06:08.300 --> 00:06:09.835
♪♪
-Krrrh!
-Come on, man.

00:06:09.835 --> 00:06:13.773
[ Laughter ]
Oh, my God.

00:06:13.773 --> 00:06:15.140
♪♪

00:06:15.140 --> 00:06:17.142
Thank you, baggage claim,

00:06:17.142 --> 00:06:19.511
for being an amusement park
for my luggage.

00:06:19.511 --> 00:06:20.579
[ Awws and applause ]

00:06:20.579 --> 00:06:22.347
Have some fun.

00:06:22.347 --> 00:06:26.585
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:26.585 --> 00:06:27.653
♪♪

00:06:27.653 --> 00:06:29.688
Thank you, Necco Wafers,

00:06:29.688 --> 00:06:31.023
or, as I like to call you,

00:06:31.023 --> 00:06:33.059
dessert Tums.
There you have it, everybody.

00:06:33.059 --> 00:06:34.060
[ Applause ]
Those are our thank-you notes.

